to infinity and beyond the wait for  disney's light year is coming to an end  so what do the great artists at disney  do for us they give us the what's what  on one of the greatest pixar characters  of all time while keeping the best  aspects of buzz we're getting an inside  look into his makeover and gadgets old  and new alright strap in for hyper speed  number one we've been promised a pixar  movie unlike any other just ask chris  evans our brand new buzz lightyear i'm a  massive fixer fan i was a kid in a candy  store the artistic team certainly wanted  to make this the most ambitious project  to honor one of the most legendary  animated characters the amount of detail  animators added for this origin story  only strengthened its foundation for  emotional storytelling they also had a  lot of time to make this one as director  angus mclean has had this one brewing  for over 20 years that's right ever  since toy story 2 angus was obsessed  with the idea of a buzz lightyear origin  story  number two reboots of old classics are  no stranger to casting different actors  for the titular roles but with light  year this one's an origin story so why  not bring back tim allen for the voice  of buzz well because they're entirely  different characters so bringing in  chris evans was not only a great idea  but his voice also really emulates  allen's interpretation censors have  detected potential life forms on an  uncharted planet it wouldn't have made  much sense to make tim the voice for the  human form just because he made the toy  version some iconic you kind of just do  a shameless tim allen impression evans  was the first and only choice to lend  his voice to this buzz but stepping into  those shoes was exciting yet  nerve-wracking for the marvel superstar  number three speaking of chris evans did  you know this is his first major  animated film yeah we were a little  surprised too just by the looks of the  trailers it seems like he's just a  natural he does have some experience  voice acting but most of his time was  spent as a hero on set this concept was  a little difficult for evans to get  through separating physical acting and  vocal but he had a great support team  throughout the process he specifically  owes it all to mclean saying so you're  really kind of leaning on the director  and angus is so wonderful you trust that  they know what they're doing and if they  say jump you just say how high and you  just try as many options as possible  number four a new buzz comes with new  characters uzu aduba joins in on the  adventure playing lightyear's first best  friend and confidant alicia hawthorne  from what we can gather from the  trailers we think she may not be in on  this one a whole lot as the plot  thickens but hawthorne's granddaughter  izzy hawthorne played by kiki palmer  takes the role and flies along the  adventure she was so thrilled to join  the team specifically a pixar team i was  so excited to jump in that world as a  fan and as an actor number five with a  great inside scoop on the plot we've  been told that buzz becomes quite the  time traveler the story begins its  second act with him traveling to another  planet little does he know that his time  is moving normally while his friends  back home are aging rapidly by the time  he comes back no the creative team is  not ripping off interstellar they  actually went through some heavy  research to get einstein's theory of  relativity right luckily they got an  interview casually scheduled with an  astronaut at the international space  station no big deal right good thing  they did because it seemed like a lot of  the team had differing opinions on the  matter right so the  faster oh boy  number six the pandemic hit hard for all  of us including the entertainment  industry but this didn't stop the light  year team at pixar they found a way to  get things done and stay on track they  brought their work home with them and  were able to come back when it was safe  to do so  number seven like marvel has its many  outtakes so do cartoons in fact light  year went through a lot of drafts for  multiple scenes they animated dozens of  unseen sequences that unfortunately will  not make it in the final cut some were  pretty necessary to take out and some  were just too hard to let go from the  story creators we've written sequences  that don't exist anymore that are just  so fun number eight sometimes you just  get a little too nervous  and start tap dancing that's exactly the  case for chris evans he excused it as  more of a way to stay occupied in the  booth saying some people whistle or chew  gum and i just kind of find myself  casually soft shoeing it's more of just  a casual thing that sometimes my feet do  without even thinking  number nine original toy story artists  had one thing in mind when designing  buzz lightyear more plastic more toy but  with the launch of the human version  artists become very picky about the  details but why it's about the birth of  a hero not a hero that became a bigger  hero there's so much more to his  appearance than meets the eye so we'll  be nitpicking his features for you as  well  number 10 there are a million different  things to worry about for this character  design but for these animators it had to  be the chin they couldn't just recycle  the old one as it's too big for human  form it took a ton of design mockups to  find the best fit we guess we can say  the original chin was just too beyond  big for anyone to consider human  number 11. we thought there was  something strange about the new buzz  where's the snood you know that purple  cap extension that he wears in toy story  right well for the design of this one  they opted for hair instead we have no  problem with that but it's just such a  staple to the iconic look goodbye great  snood we'll miss ya  number 12 who knew a hand could tell a  thousand stories the overall hand  animations really mattered during each  scene for the animators  well really the director director angus  really harps on the idea that even the  way a character presses a button tells a  lot about their overall personality they  took great care in how buzz holds his  weapons and operates machines pressing  them lightly or aggressively to propel  his emotional journey we never thought  we'd ever have an entry like this we  just really have to hand it to them for  the attention to detail  number 13. as every big budget kids  movie sells tickets they also make a lot  in merchandise and while the toy story  franchise was never a stranger to great  memorabilia lightyear intends to up the  ante a little with some of the original  gadgets like the signature wrist tech  and laser beam we get interesting new  ones as well but the gadget design isn't  what's most impressive it's all in the  belt animators spent a long time making  buzz's belt as realistic as possible  down to the ribbing in the belt buckle  all we have to say is  just shut up and take our money  number 14. what a crafty guy mclean is  his fascination with creativity knows no  bounds whenever he has an idea for  something in animation he just makes it  out of legos and with the advanced 3d  modeling software  he's able to send it to an artist and  get it rendered to a digital model one  would think working at pixar is a dream  come true but getting to play with legos  at an adult job awesome  number 15. a spin-off movie is nothing  without a few throwbacks to the original  and along with the many included in  light year we got one so subtle not a  lot of fans would really catch it that  orange suit we see buzzwearing on his  adventure is actually an ode to one of  his very first concept designs lunar  larry we're kind of glad lunar larry  didn't make it past the page lunar larry  to the rescue doesn't really give us a  whole lot of comfort but this one's  really an awesome little easter egg to  honor the great minds of toy story we  can feel safe in our minds that tim  